 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "A tiny village lost 117 shoes in one summer.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.461
  },
  {
   "text": "Every morning, another doorstep had one shoe missing. Never the pair.",
   "s": 3.761,
   "e": 7.18
  },
  {
   "text": "So the baker blamed the mailman, and the mailman blamed the baker.",
   "s": 7.48,
   "e": 10.535
  },
  {
   "text": "Until one man stayed up all night with a flashlight.",
   "s": 10.835,
   "e": 13.155
  },
  {
   "text": "At 3 a.m., something small tiptoed onto his porch.",
   "s": 13.455,
   "e": 15.832
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it grabbed his slipper and ran.",
   "s": 16.132,
   "e": 17.5
  },
  {
   "text": "He chased it into the woods. And what did he find?",
   "s": 17.8,
   "e": 20.045
  },
  {
   "text": "A fox, fast asleep on a mountain of shoes.",
   "s": 20.815,
   "e": 22.894
  },
  {
   "text": "And every single one was a left shoe.",
   "s": 23.194,
   "e": 24.838
  },
  {
   "text": "That's how a tiny village lost 117 shoes.",
   "s": 25.138,
   "e": 28.005
  }
 ],
